{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 diagnostic, after END acc70ae7: find the first differing call.\n\nThe run gave one fact. At the original cap, the production budget\nrefuses Base seq 1 at the used vector of END 755, short by one node\nof 64. The diagnostic budget confirmed the same target and used 58\nnodes. So the observer changes a budget decision, or production\ncounts an amount that the observer counts one time. The difference\nof the two vectors is the whole second entry: 1 entry, 61 attempts,\n23 nodes, 139 calls. 35 used nodes and 23 more fit in 64.\n\nNo cap, charge or assertion changes. No number of this run stands as\na minimum, a fit or an acceptance.\n\nNext, in this order.\n\n1. By a read of the retained streams and of the source, find the\n   first budget call where the two decisions differ: the call that\n   production refuses near 35 used nodes and the diagnostic admits.\n   Report the method, the requested vector, and the used, protected\n   and unsettled vectors before it, for each budget. State what the\n   depth guard of the diagnostic subclass counts one time there.\n2. If the retained ledger lacks that call, make the recorder passive\n   and run one time more: it wraps each public call of an unmodified\n   production budget from outside, records arguments and result, and\n   changes no accounting. That run must reproduce the END 755 vector\n   and the refusal at the original cap. It needs no new planner\n   grant. The stop rule of 6aafac93 holds.\n3. The Grow target and each generous pass wait for item 1.\n\nI assign the repair from item 1. Production counts one amount two\ntimes: AE-1 repairs the duplicate, with a named case. The diagnostic\ndropped a real charge: repair the diagnostic only. Neither: I take\nthe numbers to Hugh for the cap, or to ARC-1.\n\nThe slot goes on to the tooling head, P1 and E1, as 5537a531 orders.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}